OP_IRQ_SET with IRQ_SET_PERIOD on a line that fired more than a period ago
counts one period from its deadline and no further,
so a thread that woke late arms a deadline the tick has already passed.
The tick fires every due timer line,
so an Irq armed on one has its deadline ahead of the count.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: armed timer line is due

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -547,7 +547,7 @@ static uint32_t timer_period(struct irq *irq, uint32_t period)
     uint32_t now = sched_ticks;
     if (irq_due(irq, now)) {
         uint32_t behind = now - irq->deadline;
-        irq->deadline = now + period - behind % period;
+        irq->deadline += period;
         return behind / period;
     }
     irq->deadline = now + (irq->deadline - now - 1) % period + 1;
